-# Shared Bad → With OG copy for People Team, Employee, Manager (buyer order)

.marketing-persona#people
  %p.marketing-kicker People Team / HR
  %h3= local_assigns[:people_heading] || "Shoulder to shoulder ... not the form police"
  %p.marketing-bad
    There’s a special kind of joy reserved for another mandatory HR form ... the kind that takes an hour, disappears into a vault, and somehow still doesn’t help anyone know where they stand. Too often the People Team is cast as the team that protects the business from employees, instead of enabling both.
  %p.marketing-good.mb-0
    With OurGruuv, the People Team gets a system that puts them shoulder to shoulder with employees and managers ... so fairness isn’t a memory test at review time, growth isn’t only a promotion, and talent density becomes something the business can actually see rising.

.marketing-persona#employees
  %p.marketing-kicker Employees
  %h3= local_assigns[:employee_heading] || "Know where you stand"
  %p.marketing-bad
    Vague review language. “Needs more ownership” with no examples. Growth that only shows up when a title opens ... if it opens.
  %p.marketing-good.mb-0
    With OurGruuv, you get continuous clarity: what’s expected, what’s demonstrated, and how to grow beyond promotions ... not a surprise rating and a shrug.

.marketing-persona#managers
  %p.marketing-kicker Managers
  %h3= local_assigns[:manager_heading] || "Coaching with receipts"
  %p.marketing-bad
    You know someone is strong ... but when it’s time to coach or calibrate, the specifics live in your head. Feedback was given verbally and forgotten. Kudos never tied to the abilities or values that actually matter on the assignment.
  %p.marketing-good.mb-0
    With OurGruuv, managers get tools for an order of magnitude better coaching ... feedback and kudos tied to specific assignment abilities and values, so fairness and growth don’t depend on memory.
